Based upon all of the headlines you see above, filter out any headlines which do not include a number indicating increase or decrease.
For any headlines that are fluffy or fuzzy, just ignore the headline completely.
If the headline includes a number, extract the number out.
Try to determine from the surrounding text or from the number itself whether this was an increase or decrease.
If this was an increase, make the assessment in the 70% or above range.
If this was a decrease, make the assessment in the 30% or below range.

The baseline for where the SP500 is at for the start of this week is 5,686.67. So any points increase or decrease could be taken as a proportion of this.

If numbers can be gleaned from the headlines, and if the numbers are relatively high, a 1% or more, make your conviction 70% or more.

If numbers can be gleaned from the headlines, and if the numbers are relatively low, less than 1%, make your conviction 30% or less.

If no numbers can be gleaned from the headlines, make your conviction 0%.